# Obsidian per-machine state — the layout of open panes, not content.
#
# .obsidian/graph.json is deliberately not here. It holds the zoom, which is
# per-machine, and the colour groups, which are as much this vault's content as
# a board is: they are written in its own words for its own containers and
# statuses. Ignoring the file for the sake of the zoom threw away the only thing
# that makes the graph readable, so the zoom is the thing that gets committed by
# accident instead. `docket graph --colours` rewrites it and keeps your view.
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json

# Obsidian local trash
.trash/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Editors. Which panes somebody had open is not a fact about the project, and
# an .idea/ committed once follows every clone around for good.
.idea/
.vscode/
